1. Reddit-Based Research

Questions that require opinions, experiences, or discussions from Reddit:

“What are some common challenges people face when learning Python?”
“What do Reddit users recommend for staying productive while working from home?”
“What are people's biggest complaints about online learning?”
“What do travelers on Reddit say about visiting Bangalore?”
“What are the most common problems developers face when working with AWS?”
2. Structured Live Data — Open-Meteo

Questions that require current or forecasted weather information:

“What is the current temperature in Mumbai?”
“Is it going to rain in Chennai today?”
“What will the weather be like in Bangalore tomorrow?”
“What is the current weather in Delhi?”
“What is the temperature and precipitation forecast for Hyderabad?”
3. Combined Sources — Reddit + Open-Meteo

Questions where the agent needs both live weather data and Reddit opinions:

“What is the current weather in Bangalore, and what do Reddit users say about visiting the city?”
“What is the weather in Mumbai today, and do travelers on Reddit recommend visiting at this time?”
“What is the current weather in Delhi, and what experiences have Reddit users shared about traveling there?”
“How is the weather in Goa right now, and what do people on Reddit say about visiting Goa?”
“What is the current weather in Singapore, and what do Reddit users recommend doing there?”
4. Insufficient Grounding

Questions where the available Reddit and Open-Meteo sources cannot provide sufficient evidence:

“Who will win the next FIFA World Cup?”
“What is the latest version of Java?”
“Explain how quantum computing works.”
“What is the population of Chennai?”
“Who is the current CEO of Microsoft?”
“What are the best programming languages for AI?”
